Corresponding source for this exact version is published alongside the
OPad release this binary came from as tosu-4.26.2-source.tar.gz, upstream's
tree at the tag above (`make tosu-source`).

THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt lists what the binary contains besides tosu itself:
its npm production dependencies and the embedded Node.js 24 runtime.

LGPL-3.0 gives you the right to replace this component with your own
version. Point the $OSUPAD_TOSU_PATH environment variable at your own
binary to use it instead of this bundled copy.

Rebuilt component: on Linux, tosu's pp calculator (@tosuapp/lazer-calculator,
LGPL-3.0-only, https://github.com/tosuapp/lazer-calculator) is rebuilt by
OPad from the source of the exact version tosu pins, in an AlmaLinux 8
container, so that it runs on older glibc than upstream's prebuilt. The only
change is that ppy.osu.Game.Resources, taken by upstream at version "*", is
pinned to the version the pinned osu! revision names. The build script is
scripts/release/lazer-calculator/build-in-container.sh in the OPad repository,
and the calculator's source is published with each OPad release as
lazer-calculator-<version>-source.tar.gz.
